\ Bitwise-tower dogfood: pack three `u8` channels into an `i32` via `shl` + `or`
\ (the bitwise analogue of `rgb.sth`'s arithmetic pack), then unpack the green
\ channel back out via `shr` + `and`.

: pack ( i64 i64 i64 -- i32 )
  | r g b |
  r >u8 >i32 16 shl
  g >u8 >i32 8 shl or
  b >u8 >i32 or ;

: green ( i32 -- u8 )
  8 shr 255 >i32 and >u8 ;

: main ( -- )
  10 20 30 pack
  dup >i64 .          \ prints 660510
  green >i64 . ;      \ prints 20
